Analyze the context and historical background of the introduction of the term 'in-group' and 'out-group' in social psychology.
The term "in-group" and "out-group" was introduced in social psychology by Henri Tajfel and his colleagues during their work in formulating social identity theory. The concept gained popularity through the minimal group paradigm, a method used to study the significance of ingroup and outgroup categorization. This was done by creating groups of complete strangers based on trivial criteria, allowing researchers to observe the formation of in-group favoritism and out-group homogeneity.
