Based on the provided context, the current opening song performer for Monday Night Football is Hank Williams, Jr., along with country duo Florida Georgia Line and R&B singer Jason Derulo. They collaborated on a new version of the iconic opening theme song, "All My Rowdy Friends Are Here on Monday Night", which was introduced on September 11, 2017.

The history behind this tradition dates back to 1989, when Hank Williams, Jr. first reworked his country music hit "All My Rowdy Friends Are Coming Over Tonight" to be included in the telecast's introduction as "All My Rowdy Friends Are Here on Monday Night". This theme song was used until Week 3 of the 2011 season. The song was then absent from the opening sequence from Week 4 through the end of that season. In 2017, ESPN re-hired Hank Williams, Jr. for the intro, and he collaborated with Florida Georgia Line and Jason Derulo on a new version of the song.
